From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:05:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools: armprof, ARM instruction counts of the walk and the
 renderer under QEMU

The profiler that found the work in b2e0cc3..63f2059: a QEMU TCG plugin that
counts executed instructions per translated block between ge_replay's marker
functions, a do-nothing GLES2 for the ARM build, the toolchain file (the
Vita's -mcpu/-mfpu, no stack protector), and scripts that attribute the counts
to functions, callers and source lines. ge_replay already refers to it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/tools/armprof/README.md b/tools/armprof/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5f0d5fa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/armprof/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# armprof: ARM instruction counts of the GE walk and the GL renderer
+
+The PS Vita's CPU (a Cortex-A9 at 444 MHz) is where Infected's renderer was bound, and the console has no profiler we
+can attach. This directory measures the same code as an ARM program instead: `ge_replay` built for a Cortex-A9 with the
+Vita's compiler flags, a stub GLES2 that does nothing, run under QEMU's user-mode emulator with a TCG plugin that counts
+the instructions of every translated block, only between two marker functions. The counts are exact and repeatable to
+the instruction, so a change of a few thousand instructions per frame is visible; time on the console follows them at
+roughly 1.5 (walk) to 2 (renderer) cycles an instruction.
+
+`ge_replay` calls `ge_replay_profile_on/off()` around the display-list walk and `ge_replay_profile_submit_on/off()`
+around each `Renderer::submit()`; `run_prof.sh LABEL walk|submit` counts one or the other.
+
+## Setting up (once)
+
+```sh
+# QEMU with plugins (user mode, ARM only)
+git clone --depth 1 -b v8.2.2 https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu.git && cd qemu
+./configure --target-list=arm-linux-user --enable-plugins --disable-system && make -j4    # build/qemu-arm
+
+# the plugin
+gcc -O2 -shared -fPIC $(pkg-config --cflags glib-2.0) -I qemu/include/qemu tbcount.c -o libtbcount.so
+
+# an ARM sysroot with zlib and the stub GL (Ubuntu: gcc-arm-linux-gnueabihf, g++-arm-linux-gnueabihf)
+export ARMPROF_SYSROOT=$PWD/sysroot
+arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc -O2 -mcpu=cortex-a9 -mfpu=neon -mfloat-abi=hard -mthumb -I<GLES2/EGL headers> -c stub_gl.c
+arm-linux-gnueabihf-ar rcs $ARMPROF_SYSROOT/lib/libstubgl.a stub_gl.o
+# (zlib: configure with CC=arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc --static --prefix=$ARMPROF_SYSROOT)
+
+# the ARM ge_replay (static, -O3, the Vita's -mcpu/-mfpu, no stack protector or fortify as VitaSDK has neither)
+cmake -S <PortableKit> -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=$PWD/toolchain.cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+      -DPORTABLEKIT_GE_REPLAY=ON -DPORTABLEKIT_GL_RENDERER=ON -DPORTABLEKIT_RENDERER=OFF \
+      -DPORTABLEKIT_GL_INCLUDE_DIR=<GLES2/EGL headers> -DPORTABLEKIT_GL_LIBRARIES=$ARMPROF_SYSROOT/lib/libstubgl.a
+cmake --build build --target ge_replay
+```
+
+## Measuring
+
+```sh
+export ARMPROF_BUILD=$PWD/build QEMU=$PWD/qemu/build/qemu-arm
+./run_prof.sh base submit <dump dir>             # the renderer's own work per frame, by function
+./run_prof.sh base walk <dump dir>               # the walk (with the renderer inline)
+./run_prof.sh prep submit <dump dir> --prepare   # the GL thread's share when the split renderer prepares draws
+./run_calls.sh c1 submit <dump dir> memset __aeabi_uidivmod   # who calls these, per frame
+python3 lines.py build/bin/ge_replay tb_base_submit_r1.out tb_base_submit_r3.out 20 "GlRenderer::Impl::submit(" 40
+```
+
+Each run replays the flips twice (`--repeat 1` and `3`) and reports the difference per frame, so loading the dump and
+first-use costs (program links, texture decodes) cancel out. `lines.py` splits one function's count by source line,
+both by the innermost (inlined) line and by the function's own line it was inlined at.
+
+The plugin is built against QEMU's plugin API header (GPL-2.0-or-later); it is a development tool, not part of what a
+port links.
diff --git a/tools/armprof/attribute.py b/tools/armprof/attribute.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3004629
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/armprof/attribute.py
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+"""attribute.py BINARY TB_R1 TB_R3 FRAMES: per-frame instruction counts by function, from two tbcount runs (r3 - r1)."""
+import bisect, subprocess, sys
+binary, a_path, b_path, frames = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], float(sys.argv[4])
+syms = []
+for line in subprocess.run(['arm-linux-gnueabihf-nm', '-C', '--defined-only', '-S', '--numeric-sort', binary], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.splitlines():
+    parts = line.split(' ', 3)
+    if len(parts) < 4 or parts[2] not in 'tTwW': continue
+    addr = int(parts[0], 16) & ~1; size = int(parts[1], 16)
+    syms.append((addr, size, parts[3]))
+syms.sort()
+starts = [s[0] for s in syms]
+def fn(pc):
+    i = bisect.bisect_right(starts, pc) - 1
+    if i < 0: return '?'
+    a, s, n = syms[i]
+    return n if pc < a + max(s, 2) else '?' + hex(pc)
+def load(path):
+    d = {}
+    for line in open(path):
+        pc, n, e, m = line.split()
+        pc = int(pc, 16); n = int(n); e = int(e); m = int(m)
+        name = fn(pc)
+        ins, mem = d.get(name, (0, 0))
+        d[name] = (ins + n * e, mem + m)
+    return d
+a = load(a_path); b = load(b_path)
+rows = []
+for k, (ins, mem) in b.items():
+    ia, ma = a.get(k, (0, 0))
+    rows.append(((ins - ia) / frames, (mem - ma) / frames, k))
+rows.sort(reverse=True)
+total = sum(r[0] for r in rows)
+print(f'total ARM instructions per frame: {total:,.0f}')
+groups = {}
+for ins, mem, k in rows:
+    pass
+skip = ('inflate', 'adler32', 'gedump::', 'zcalloc', 'zcfree', 'crc32', 'fread', '_IO_', 'uncompress')
+kept = [r for r in rows if not any(s in r[2] for s in skip)]
+ktotal = sum(r[0] for r in kept)
+print(f'excluding dump loading: {ktotal:,.0f} instructions, {sum(r[1] for r in kept):,.0f} memory accesses per frame')
+for ins, mem, k in kept[:60]:
+    print(f'{ins:12,.0f} {mem:11,.0f} {100*ins/ktotal:5.1f}%  {k[:140]}')
diff --git a/tools/armprof/callers.py b/tools/armprof/callers.py
new file mode 100644
